sections.purpose_text:
We process your data for the following purposes:
• handling inquiries submitted via the contact form (name, email, phone number, message) — to respond and establish cooperation;
• performing surveying contracts — to the extent required to deliver the service;
• website traffic analysis — only after you grant consent in the cookie banner (see “Cookies and analytics”);
• ensuring website security and proper operation — including remembering your language preference and your cookie choice.

sections.legal_text:
We process your data on the following legal grounds:
• Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR — your freely given consent (contact form, analytics cookies);
• Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR — performance of a contract or taking pre-contractual steps (surveying assignments);
• Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR — our legitimate interest (website security, essential cookies, archiving correspondence to defend against potential claims).

sections.retention_text:
We keep your data no longer than necessary:
• contact-form data — up to 24 months from the last contact;
• contract-related data — for the statutory archiving period (up to 5 years from the end of the financial year);
• analytics cookies (Google Analytics 4) — up to 14 months from the last activity;
• essential cookies — until the browser session ends or for up to 12 months.

sections.recipients_text:
Your data may be shared with the following categories of recipients:
• Vercel Inc. — website hosting provider (under a data-processing agreement);
• Google Ireland Limited / Google LLC — Google Analytics 4 provider (only with your consent);
• n8n GmbH — automation of contact-form notifications;
• Google (Gmail), Meta Platforms (WhatsApp Business) — channels that receive new-inquiry notifications;
• law firms and architectural offices cooperating on a specific project — only to the extent necessary to perform the contract.
We do not sell your data and do not share it with third parties for marketing purposes.

sections.rights_text:
Regarding our processing of your data, you have the right to:
• access your data and obtain a copy;
• rectify (correct) inaccurate or outdated data;
• erase your data (“the right to be forgotten”);
• restrict processing;
• object to processing;
• data portability to another controller;
• withdraw consent at any time — without affecting the lawfulness of processing carried out on the basis of consent before its withdrawal;
• lodge a complaint with the supervisory authority — the President of the Personal Data Protection Office (Stawki 2, 00-193 Warsaw, uodo.gov.pl).
